# Built binaries. `go build` with no -o writes one named after the package into
# the working tree, and one sweeping add later it is in the history of every
# clone for ever. That has happened in this fleet: 22 MB, and the history had
# to be rewritten to get it out.
/gitpush
/ghmerge
/ghscopes
/git-pre-push-guard
/git-credential-tokenfile
/cmd/*/gitpush
/cmd/*/ghscopes
/cmd/*/git-pre-push-guard
/cmd/*/git-credential-tokenfile
/ghrelease
/credscan
/cmd/*/credscan
/git-post-checkout-guard
/cmd/*/git-post-checkout-guard
# ⛔ Added 2026-10-31 after `go build ./cmd/guardscan/` dropped a 5.1 MB binary
# in the root and one `git add -A` committed it. Caught before the push went
# anywhere by reading the commit's own file list, not by this file — which is
# the point worth keeping: THIS LIST NAMES BINARIES ONE BY ONE, so it is always
# one command behind, and it was never the barrier. The barrier is the CI gate
# "nothing big is tracked". Build with `-o` into the scratchpad instead.
/guardscan
/cmd/*/guardscan
/hookcheck
/cmd/*/hookcheck
/guard-bash
/cmd/*/guard-bash
/ghnew
/cmd/*/ghnew
/ghpkg
/cmd/*/ghpkg
/ghrunner
/cmd/*/ghrunner
/glscopes
/cmd/*/glscopes
/glci
/cmd/*/glci
/reauthor
/cmd/*/reauthor
